{
	quest.0132FF111070733C.quest_desc: [
		"Status Moves are moves that do not inflict direct damage in battle, and instead either grant the user an advtantage such as a stat boost or protection with moves such as Swords dance, Protect or Light Screen or impose a disadvantage on the opponent such as status conditions or field conditions with moves such as Thunder Wave, Rain Dance or Sticky Webs"
		""
		"Status moves are not affected by a Pokemon's stats, however their use can be influenced by abilities such as Prankster which allows the user to use a status move first in battle, or magic bounce which reflects status moves back to the user."
	]
	quest.0132FF111070733C.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Status TM/TR"
	quest.0132FF111070733C.title: "Status Moves"
	quest.0B25D44D32C636C3.quest_desc: ["Dynamax is a phenomenon that allows your Pokemon to grow to extreme sizes! This grants the Pokemon access to Dynamax moves, and boosts the Pokemon's health massively. This can only be done around a \"Power Spot\" and you can only Dynamax/Gigantamax one Pokemon on your team per battle."]
	quest.0B25D44D32C636C3.quest_subtitle: "Dynamax a Pokemon!"
	quest.0B25D44D32C636C3.title: "Dynamax"
	quest.0E86F0699B54BE28.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to the World of Competitive Pokemon!"
	quest.1158ECC5643EED01.quest_desc: ["The Tera Type of a Pokemon can be changed by right clicking the pokemon with 50 Tera Shards of the type you wish to change to in your hand"]
	quest.1158ECC5643EED01.quest_subtitle: "Change the Tera Type of a Pokemon"
	quest.1960E2C9294C431A.quest_desc: ["Z-Moves are extremely powerful moves that can only be used once per battle, so choose when to use it wisely. These moves require the Pokemon to hold a specific Z-Crystal depending on the Pokemon or the type of move."]
	quest.1960E2C9294C431A.quest_subtitle: "Use a Z-Move"
	quest.1960E2C9294C431A.title: "Z-Moves"
	quest.1B209526840B2E63.quest_desc: [
		"But what do you do if you accidentally raise an EV by too much, or raise an EV you didn't even want to raise?"
		"Well that's where Berries come in!"
		""
		"Each Berry will decrease an EV by 10 points for it's corresponding stat:"
		"- Kelpsey Berry decreases Attack"
		"- Qualot Berry decreases Defence"
		"- Hondew Berry decreases Special Attack"
		"- Grepa Berry decreases Special Defence"
		"- Pomeg Berry decreases HP"
		"- Tomato Berry decreases Speed"
		""
		"Now you know everything you need to EV train your Pokemon and make them as powerful as they can be!"
	]
	quest.1B209526840B2E63.quest_subtitle: "Obtain Each EV Berry"
	quest.1B209526840B2E63.title: "EV Berries"
	quest.20103EF952C7F91A.quest_desc: [
		"The best way of obtaining a Pokemon with optimal IVs is through Breeding."
		"Breeding for IVs involves using two parents in the same egg group that have IVs that you want, and the best way to make the most of this is using EV training items and the Destiny Knot."
		""
		"EV training items, when held by one of the parents, will garuntee that its IVs of its respective stat will be passed down to the child."
		"For example if you had a parent with 31 IVs in attack, giving it the Power Bracer will garuntee that those 31 Attack IVs will be passed to the Child."
		"You would then have the other parent hold a different EV training item to get a different stat, or you can use a Destiny knot."
		""
		"The Destiny Knot is a very powerful breeding tool as it passes down FIVE IVs from either parent down to the child. "
		""
		"NOTE: It's important to remember that the Destiny Knot does NOT necessarily pass down 5 of the IVs of the parent that holds it, rather it can take 5 IVs from BOTH PARENTS, and it is RANDOM. This means that it could pass down 3 IVs from one parent, and 2 from the other. "
		""
		"This method works best when you have a 5IV Parent (so a Pokemon with 5 maxed out IVs, lets say max everything other than speed) and another 5IV Pokemon that specifically has a maxed out stat that you are missing, in this example Speed. You can optimise your chances of getting a 6IV pokemon by giving the first 5IV Parent the Destiny knot, then giving the other Parent the Power Anklet. This means that you are getting a garunteed 5IVs passed down to the child, plus the maximum speed. Granted this does not garuntee you a 6IV pokemon because the stats being chosen by the Destiny knot are still RANDOM"
	]
	quest.20103EF952C7F91A.quest_subtitle: "Breeding to Improve IVs"
	quest.20103EF952C7F91A.title: "Breeding"
	quest.21958D9AFC8F8F56.quest_desc: [
		"Every Pokemon has a unique Base Stat Total that is a total of the Pokemons other stats: HP, Attack, Defence, Speed, Special Attack and Special Defence. These stats CANNOT be changed. "
		""
		"The base stats of a Pokemon make up the foundation of a Pokemon's stats that can be built on through various means, the first being Natures. Natures influence the Pokemon's stats by providing a 10% increase to one stat, and a 10% decrease to another. "
		""
		"For example, a Pokemon with the Adamant nature will receive a 10% increase in ATTACK, with a 10% decrease in SPECIAL ATTACK. This is useful for Pokemon with a good base attack stats and access to decent physical moves, or for Pokemon that don't need their special attack stat."
		""
		"There are some Natures such as Docile or Serious that provide no changes whatsoever."
	]
	quest.267B8277A2ED299F.quest_desc: ["Equipping a Z-Ring allows your Pokemon to use Z-Moves in battle."]
	quest.267B8277A2ED299F.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Z Ring!"
	quest.267B8277A2ED299F.title: "Z Ring"
	quest.2B6D7ED85A207B54.quest_desc: [
		"Effort Values are by far the most important stats a pokemon can have, while also being the stat that you have the most control over."
		""
		"A Pokemon can have a maximum of 510 EVs, split across it's 6 stats, where an individual stat can have a maximum of 255 points attributed to it."
		"EVs will increase a Pokemons stat by 1 per 4 EVs, so 4 EVs in attack will increase the Pokemon's total attack stat by 1 point."
		""
		"Every Pokemon when caught will start off with 0 EVs, a blank slate for you to do whatever you wish with."
		"EVs can be altered through a few methods:"
		"- Increase via battling"
		"- Increase via vitamins/feathers"
		"- Decrease via berries."
		""
		"Let's explore these more."
	]
	quest.2B6D7ED85A207B54.quest_subtitle: "Effort Values"
	quest.30191941E0D84FCB.quest_desc: [
		"Stats are extremely important in Pokemon. They determine how hard your Pokemon hits, how well it can take a hit and how fast it moves. "
		""
		"Stats are made up of four Components:"
		"- Base Stat Total (BST)"
		"- Nature"
		"- Effort Values (EVs)"
		"- Indivisual Values (IVs)"
		""
		"Let's Explore these in more detail."
	]
	quest.30191941E0D84FCB.quest_subtitle: "Learn About Pokemon Stats!"
	quest.3CE548B5CB0162B0.quest_desc: ["A Pokemon's Nature can be changed through the use of Mints. Mints are cratfed using Mint Leaves which can be found growing around the world. To craft a mint, you simply take three of the mint colour that represents the stat you want to increase (for example red for attack) with one of the colour representing the stat you want to decrease (for example Cyan for Special Attack) and this will craft a singular mint that you can feed to your Pokemon"]
	quest.3CE548B5CB0162B0.quest_subtitle: "Obtain All the Mint Leaves!"
	quest.3CE548B5CB0162B0.title: "Mint Leaves"
	quest.3DBB8084AA753753.quest_desc: [
		"Blank TMs allow you to copy a move from a Pokemon onto the TM. This creates a TM of that move that you can then use on other Pokemon."
		""
		"TMs can be used multiple times."
	]
	quest.3DBB8084AA753753.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Blank TM"
	quest.3EDDFFC0CE864EC4.quest_desc: [
		"Every wild Pokemon When defeated will give a number of EVs, usually ranging from 1 to 3, for a specific stat. The number of EVs given typically changes based on the evolutionary stage of a Pokemon. For example a Wooper will give 1 HP EV, while a Quagsire will give 2 HP EVs. "
		""
		"There are hundreds of resources online detailing what EVs each Pokemon provides when defeated, so if you plan to use this method research which Pokemon you need to defeat!"
		""
		"This process can be made much easier however with the use of EV Training Items. These are Held items that provide extra EVs for each wild Pokemon you defeat, in addition to the EVs already provided by the wild Pokemon."
		"- Power Anklet will give 4 Speed EVs"
		"- Power Lens will give 4 Special Attack EVs"
		"- Power Bracer will give 4 Attack EVs"
		"- Power Weight will give 4 HP EVs"
		"- Power Belt will give 4 Defence EVs"
		"- Power Band will give 4 Special Defence EVs"
		""
		"This means that if your Pokemon is holding a Power Bracer, and defeats a wild Wooper, your Pokemon will gain 1 HP EV, and 4 Attack EVs"
	]
	quest.3EDDFFC0CE864EC4.quest_subtitle: "Obtain Each of the EV Training Items"
	quest.3EDDFFC0CE864EC4.title: "EV Training"
	quest.3FEC404D6D073128.quest_desc: [
		"Physical Attacks are moves used by Pokemon that typically make some sort of contact with the opposing Pokemon. This includes moves such as Earthquake, Fire Fang or Aerial Ace."
		""
		"Physical Attacks utilise the users Attack stat and work against the opponents Defence stat."
	]
	quest.3FEC404D6D073128.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Physical TM/TR"
	quest.3FEC404D6D073128.title: "Physical Attacks"
	quest.44C07815767ED43A.quest_desc: ["Equipping a Tera Orb allows your Pokemon to activate it's Tera Type in battle. "]
	quest.44C07815767ED43A.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Tera Orb!"
	quest.47196875B4D3FA38.quest_desc: [
		"Special Attacks are moves used by Pokemon that inflict special damage. These moves do not involve making physical contact with the opponent. This includes moves such as Thunderbolt, Ice Beam and Shadow Ball."
		""
		"Special Attacks utilise the users Special Attack stat against the opponents Special Defence stat"
	]
	quest.47196875B4D3FA38.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Special TM/TR"
	quest.47196875B4D3FA38.title: "Special Attacks"
	quest.494DBD7A03244EB1.quest_desc: [
		"Individual Values (IVs) are essentially the Pokemon's Genes and as such cannot be changed. IVs are values that range from 0-31 for each individual stat, where the higher the value, the better the stat. "
		""
		"In most cases you ideally want 31 in each stat, however there are a few exceptions to this, such as Pokemon that benefit from being as slow as possible (Gyro ball users, Trick Room teams) or Special attackers who benefit from having a low as possible attack stat to take minimal damage from moves such as Foul Play. "
		""
		"The only way to get better IVs on a Pokemon is to either catch a Pokemon that already has good IVs, or through breeding."
	]
	quest.494DBD7A03244EB1.quest_subtitle: "Individual Values"
	quest.55619B47364C80AD.quest_desc: [
		"\"Gimmicks\" are techniques used in Pokemon battles to give your Pokemon some type of advtantage, through the use of special items and abilities. "
		""
		"The four Gimmicks currently in Pokemon include: Dynamax, Mega Evolution, Terastalisation and Z-Moves"
	]
	quest.55619B47364C80AD.quest_subtitle: "Learn about battle \"Gimmicks\""
	quest.5AD72525A0B28903.quest_desc: [
		"Pokemon Moves are Abilties able to be used by a Pokemon in Battle. Each Pokemon has a wide variety of Moves it can learn, however it is limited to only knowing four at a time. Pokemon Learn moves in 3 ways: Level up, Egg Moves and TR/TMs"
		""
		"Pokemon Moves come in 3 types: "
		"- Physical"
		"- Special"
		"- Status"
		""
		"Let's learn some more about these."
	]
	quest.5AD72525A0B28903.quest_subtitle: "Learn a Little about Pokemon Moves"
	quest.5BAD9FC2D88DE051.quest_desc: ["Additonally to Vitamins, there are also Feathers, which provide 1 EV each for their respective stat"]
	quest.5BAD9FC2D88DE051.quest_subtitle: "Obtain Each Feather"
	quest.5BAD9FC2D88DE051.title: "EV Feathers"
	quest.5D846812F395F507.quest_desc: [
		"Vitamins are a far easier way of increasing a Pokemons EVs. Each Vitamin provides 10 EVs for the stat it represents:"
		"- Protein for Attack"
		"- Calcium for Special Attack"
		"- Iron for Defence"
		"- Zinc for Special Defence"
		"- HP Up for HP"
		"- Carbos for Speed"
	]
	quest.5D846812F395F507.quest_subtitle: "Obtain Each Vitamin"
	quest.5D846812F395F507.title: "EV Vitamins"
	quest.5DD8A869827AA109.quest_desc: ["The Omni ring is a Z Ring, Dynamx Band, Mega Bracelet and Tera Orb all in one..."]
	quest.5DD8A869827AA109.quest_subtitle: "Obtain the Omni Ring!"
	quest.626F75EFC4377E16.quest_desc: [
		"Abilities are special attributes given to Pokemon that can give them unique skills in battle, such as providing immunities, giving stat boosts or changing the Pokemon's form. Each Pokemon can only have 1 ability at a time, but most have a small range of Abilities/Hidden Abilities that they can choose between, though changing a Pokemon's ability requires the use of an Ability Capsule (which will cycle through a {Pokemon's regular Abilities), or an Abilitiy Patch (which will change a Pokemon's Ability to it's Hidden Ability) "
		""
		"Hidden Abilities are rarer, typically more powerful Abilities that most Pokemon have access to. Typically each Pokemon will have one hidden ability, and most hidden abilities are different for each Pokemon. Once a Pokemon's ability has been changed to its Hidden Ability using an ability patch, it cannot be changed back."
	]
	quest.626F75EFC4377E16.quest_subtitle: "Obtain Ability Changing Items"
	quest.626F75EFC4377E16.title: "Abilities"
	quest.65867C101F47042B.quest_desc: [
		"Blank TRs allow you to copy a move from a Pokemon onto the TR. This creates a TR of that move that you can then use on other Pokemon."
		""
		"TRs can only be used once."
	]
	quest.65867C101F47042B.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Blank TR"
	quest.661AB1BF59414382.quest_desc: [
		"Terastalisation changes the Pokemon's typing for the duration of the battle, giving it extra STAB (Same Type Attack Bonus) damage on that type, along with the original type(s) of the Pokemon. You can only Terastalise one Pokemon on your team per battle."
		""
		"Make sure to heal after each use, as Terastalisation uses charges on the Tera Orb, which can be recharged using a Healing Machine"
	]
	quest.661AB1BF59414382.quest_subtitle: "Terastalise Any Pokemon!"
	quest.661AB1BF59414382.title: "Terastalisation"
	quest.685A43C9C91EB6C7.quest_desc: ["PP up and PP max are used to increase the amount of PP that a Pokemon's move has, thus increasing the amount of times that it can be used in battle"]
	quest.685A43C9C91EB6C7.quest_subtitle: "hehe PP"
	quest.73F6786400559270.quest_desc: ["Equipping a Mega Bracelet will allow your Pokemon to Mega Evolve in battle."]
	quest.73F6786400559270.quest_subtitle: "Obtain A Mega Bracelet!"
	quest.73F6786400559270.title: "Mega Bracelet"
	quest.75AA9D930B394904.quest_desc: ["Equipping a Dynamax Band allows your Pokemon to Dynamax in battle."]
	quest.75AA9D930B394904.quest_subtitle: "Obtain a Dynamax Band!"
	quest.7C6E2BBC38B703C4.quest_desc: ["Mega Evolution is a temporary form of evolution that unlocks new power in certain Pokemon, making them more powerful than they were before! You can only Mega Evolve one Pokemon on your team per battle."]
	quest.7C6E2BBC38B703C4.quest_subtitle: "Mega Evolve any Pokemon!"
	quest.7C6E2BBC38B703C4.title: "Mega Evolution"
	quest.7D1871C9C8A2447A.quest_desc: ["Gigantamax is a form of Dynamax unique to a few Pokemon. While also making them big, it gives them a new form and access to unique Max Moves"]
	quest.7D1871C9C8A2447A.quest_subtitle: "Gigantamax a Pokemon!"
	quest.7D1871C9C8A2447A.title: "Gigantamax"
